        "original_id": "76dc1a84-692a-59e9-9621-2cb14abb6992",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Robin Hood (1973 film), Oz the Great and Powerful, Turn Off the Moon, The Jungle Book, The Aristocats\n- People: Phil Harris, Sam Raimi, Joe Roth, David Lindsay-Abaire, Mitchell Kapner, Charlie Ruggles, Eleanore Whitney, Johnny Downs, Kenny Baker, Ben Blue\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: Director, Producer, Screenwriters, Cast\n\nFacts:\n- The Jungle Book was released in 1967, and Phil Harris played Baloo the bear in it.\n- The Aristocats was released in 1970, and Phil Harris played Thomas O'Malley in it.\n- Robin Hood is a 1973 American animated musical comedy-adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- Robin Hood was first released in the United States on November 8, 1973.\n- Phil Harris played Little John in Robin Hood.\n- Turn Off the Moon stars Charlie Ruggles, Eleanore Whitney, Johnny Downs, Kenny Baker, Phil Harris, and Ben Blue.\n- Oz the Great and Powerful is a 2013 American fantasy adventure film directed by Sam Raimi and produced by Joe Roth.\n- Oz the Great and Powerful was written by David Lindsay-Abaire and Mitchell Kapner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
